// EcTerrainOverrides.kdl
//
// Purpose:
// - User-editable integration/override table for EC terrain materials.
// - The EC land packer embeds it in `tex_land_ec.uddp` as
//   `metadata/terrain_overrides.json` (this shipped copy, or the one given with
//   `--land-terrain-overrides-kdl`), and packs the textures it references.
// - The app reads only that embedded copy, so an edit takes effect after a
//   repack. The app package does not ship this file; the tools package keeps
//   it in `shared/cc_ec_convtables/`.
// - Use this only for reviewed facts or user policy choices that are not
//   currently derivable from original EC source files.
//
// Source-of-truth rule:
// - `TerrainDefinition.uop` and packed terrain provenance remain authoritative
//   for source-derived aliases, layers, selected primary textures, and stretch.
// - This file integrates or overrides that data. It must not become a duplicate
//   handwritten copy of everything that the packer already derives.
//
// Top-level syntax:
//
//     terrain MATERIAL_ID {
//         ...
//     }
//
// - `MATERIAL_ID`: unsigned integer. EC terrain material/runtime slot id.
// - Multiple `terrain MATERIAL_ID` blocks are allowed. Their children merge in
//   file order for the same id.
//
// Supported child nodes:
//
// There are no `policy` or `liquid` nodes. Neither had a client basis: edge
// softness is each material's TerrainDefinition.uop `coverage_exponent` (no
// "smooth" policy), and a water material scrolls its distortion map (item 0) by
// its tweaks 0/1 per second (UOWaterTerrainLayer::Draw; no "follow-center"
// policy, no liquid speed or wave height). The renderer reads both directly.
//
// 1. `layer`
//
//     layer "t0" tex=2000510 stretch=5.0 code="reviewed_layer_texture"
//
// - Argument: role string.
// - Known role strings used by the current material model:
//   - `"t0"`: base/albedo layer.
//   - `"t1"`: detail/secondary albedo layer.
//   - `"m"`: mask/alpha blend-control layer.
//   - `"s"`: support/specular-like or future support role.
//   - `"n"`: normal-map-like support role.
// - `t0`, `t1`, `m` and `n` override render layers 0, 1, 2 and 3. Any other
//   role string (including `s`) takes the layer at its position among the
//   material's `layer` overrides.
// - The source items bind by position per layer class (TerrainLayerClass in
//   lib/uocf terrain_definition.rs): default/bump `t0`/`t1`/`m` = items 0/1/2
//   (colour = item0 · a + item1 · (1 − a), a = item 2 alpha); water `t0` =
//   item 1 (fallback colour), `n` = item 0 (distortion du/dv), and the main
//   colour is item 2 (no override role).
// - Properties:
//   - `tex`: required unsigned integer EC texture id.
//   - `stretch`: optional float. Authored repetition/stretch. Preserve source
//     values when known; wrong stretch makes large textures shrink into one tile.
//   - `code`: optional short reason code.
//
// 2. `texture`
//
//     texture 1269 role="base" code="reviewed_textureid"
//
// - Argument: unsigned integer EC texture id.
// - Properties:
//   - `role`: optional free-form role string, useful for metadata and future
//     diagnostics. Common values are `"base"`, `"detail"`, `"mask"`,
//     `"normal"`, `"support"`. `base`, `detail`, `mask` and `normal` stand in
//     for material layers 0, 1, 2 and 3 when no `layer` override sets them.
//   - `code`: optional short reason code.
// - Use `texture` when a reviewed texture relationship must be preserved but it
//   is not yet tied to a concrete runtime layer override.
//
// 3. `ignore`
//
//     ignore code="intentionally_hidden"
//
// - Marks this material as intentionally hidden/ignored by policy.
// - Use sparingly. This should be reserved for reviewed no-render cases, not for
//   unresolved parser bugs.
// - `code`: optional short reason code.
//
// Reason code guidance:
// - Keep `code` values short, enumerable, and machine-greppable.
// - No codes are in use (the file has no entries).
// - Suggested codes when needed:
//   - `reviewed_layer_texture`
//   - `reviewed_textureid`
//   - `intentionally_hidden`
//   - `not_derivable_from_source`
//   - `manual_visual_match`
//
// Relationship to other KDL files:
// - `TerrainTranscode.kdl` maps CC land ids to EC terrain/runtime slots.
// - `EcTerrainOverrides.kdl` modifies/integrates EC terrain material behavior.
// - `EcSurfaceOverrides.kdl` handles surface-like item/static art routing.
//
// Earlier versions of this file are in git history.
//
// Removed entries:
// - Terrains 5 (water), 10 (lava), 49 (acid) and 70 (swamp) had `liquid`
//   speed/wave values (never read by the renderer) and `t0`/`n` layers that
//   equalled the source water items 1 and 0, which the renderer binds by
//   position for every water material. They first mirrored the third-party
//   UOClient-stefanomerotta terrain data.
// - Terrain 52 ("tan no-name", classic NoName land 76..) drew the obsidian
//   textures of material 51 (02000510/02000511 at stretch 5) instead of its
//   source items (02000520 twice, mask 01000003). The client draws the source
//   items, so the entry is gone.
//
// The file has no entries: every EC terrain material draws its
// TerrainDefinition.uop items. Add `terrain` blocks after this comment only
// for reviewed facts the source data does not carry.
